WEBVTT

00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:14,320
Hello, everyone. This is Anne with Connors Clinic, and today we're going to talk about B vitamins.

00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:20,000
B vitamins are a key player in maintaining optimal health and keeping you energized.

00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,200
They catalyze numerous metabolic reactions throughout the body by acting as coal enzymes for

00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:31,760
the release of energy. And the energy that is released with the assistance of B vitamins is called ATP.

00:00:32,480 --> 00:00:38,720
ATP is what our cells use, again, as energy to perform all of their complicated functions.

00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:45,120
B vitamins are made up of eight different vitamins that are water-soluble, and this means that

00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:51,040
they're excreted from the body on a daily basis, and so they must be replenished. How do we

00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:56,800
replenish our B vitamins? Well, we get them from the variety of different fruits and vegetables that

00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:02,240
we eat, from the foods that we eat, and we also can produce them through our gut microbiome.

00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:08,080
So if you're not eating a healthy Whole Foods diet, or if you have gut dysbiosis, chances are

00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:13,680
you're not getting adequate B vitamins. And here's just kind of a list of some of the functions

00:01:13,680 --> 00:01:20,080
that B vitamins are involved in helping to regulate the thyroid, helping support the immune system,

00:01:20,080 --> 00:01:25,440
protecting the heart and blood vessels, reducing the risk of developing cataracts.

00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:30,880
B vitamins help support healthy hair skin and nails, and they help regulate stress and mood.

00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:37,920
